1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
CareCompanion — medication safety guardrails for Alexa+

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:14,500
Eleanor is 78 and takes five medications. Her daughter Priya lives two hours away.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
"Alexa, what's my plan today?"

4
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:39,500
MCP tools/call · get_todays_plan — the briefing comes straight from the MCP server

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
"I took my blood pressure pill, the lisinopril."

6
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:58,000
Duplicate-dose guard: the server refuses until it hears an explicit yes AND a reason

7
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:09,500
Override recorded — flagged to Priya with the reason, visible on the dashboard

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
"I'm feeling a bit dizzy this morning."

9
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:34,500
Symptom escalation: urgent → priority-1 caregiver notified (notification simulated)

10
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Caregiver adds ibuprofen → interaction check: Warfarin (major), Lisinopril (moderate) — informational, with a disclaimer

11
00:01:50,200 --> 00:02:04,500
Every alert closed by a caregiver leaves an audit trail

12
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:18,000
One MCP server: 8 tools · 1 resource · 1 prompt · dashboard shipped as an MCP App

13
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:29,500
Agent Skill drives the same server from any agent · classic Alexa Skill front end · Bedrock or rule brain

14
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Open source, MIT · github.com/skiitk2510/carecompanion · coordination and reminders, not medical advice
